40yd|n|The expanse of space surrounding the earth; esp., that which seems to be over the earth like a great arch or dome; the firmament; the sky; the place where the sun, moon, and stars appear; -- often used in the plural in this sense. ; The dwelling place of the Deity; the abode of bliss; the place or state of the blessed after death. ; The sovereign of heaven; God; also, the assembly of the blessed, collectively; -- used variously in this sense, as in No. 2. ; Any place of supreme happiness or great comfort; perfect felicity; bliss; a sublime or exalted condition; as, a heaven of delight.	a:9wuh,133,25;a2bj,129,24;2v1r,87,2;76l1,76,39;8k4j,53,31;30eo,41,25;6849,40,47;8xpz,37,21;1hx3,35,32;8qcn,34,9;5epm,33,44;43bk,29,49;9lrd,27,164;43ai,10,82;a4ek,9,3~69ri,3,506;9lrd,27,164;43ai,10,82;43bk,29,49;6849,40,47;5epm,33,44;76l1,76,39;1hx3,35,32;8k4j,53,31;5eo7,2,29;9wuh,133,25;30eo,41,25;8800,8,25;a2bj,129,24;8xpz,37,21	v:mld,42,3;2x3v,23,24;7r1j,11,5;30eo,4,2~2x3v,23,24;7r1j,11,5;mld,42,3;30eo,4,2	V:3cdt,77,34;8m51,63,2;7vgy,62,1;3y19,57,2;8yd3,38,1;6pgw,27,1;37oc,26,10;2cg7,17,1;3ehc,15,2~3cdt,77,34;37oc,26,10;3ehc,15,2;3y19,57,2;8m51,63,2;6pgw,27,1;7vgy,62,1;8yd3,38,1;2cg7,17,1	n:a2bj,116,10;33f1,74,14;9s0b,43,77;3b4d,42,1;76l1,39,3;aqjh,38,1;a106,22,319;9fez,8,12;8k4j,3,1;w46,3,181~a106,22,319;w46,3,181;9s0b,43,77;33f1,74,14;9fez,8,12;a2bj,116,10;76l1,39,3;3b4d,42,1;8k4j,3,1;aqjh,38,1	N:g3j,33,2;2y2x,32,2;3eho,12,1;80vh,7,2;3ehc,5,1;41gl,2,3~41gl,2,3;g3j,33,2;80vh,7,2;2y2x,32,2;3eho,12,1;3ehc,5,1
